Subject: [PATCH 01385/11362] [conductor] Pre-gate block: VERIFIER-AS-REWARD
 RFT -- EVAL + GATE (THE PIVOT, part 3; the DE-CONFOUNDED gate): poll
 exp4078's training; PER LADDER BASE, once its arms have usable checkpoints,
 EVAL each on the HELD-OUT ARC-induction split (disjoint from train) and
 report demo-perfect + true-gold induction rate for Arm A (RFT-correct), Arm B
 (RFT-ablation), Arm C (gold-SFT), the BASE's OWN cold rate (measured), and
 CODEX (~0.57 ceiling). THE LOAD-BEARING GATE is A vs B (the verifier-LABEL
 test): does RFT-CORRECT beat RFT-ABLATION on held-out induction with
 bootstrap CI95 excluding 0? If YES -> the verifier's LABEL carries training
 signal (verifier-as-reward is REAL, not codex-distillation). If A~=B -> 'RFT
 helps' is just codex-distillation; the verifier adds nothing (the honest null
 -- report it plainly, do NOT dress it as a win). SECONDARY: A vs C (does the
 label-free verifier signal match oracle labels -- A>=C?) and A vs cold base
 (any lift at all). ROBUSTNESS: report all three contrasts PER base; the
 headroom rung (Qwen3.5-0.8B) is PRIMARY; A>B holding ACROSS the ladder =
 robust. CAPACITY-FLOOR GUARD: a base whose cold rate is 0 is dropped as
 uninformative (NOT 'verifier fails'); if all bases floor, fall back to the
 Sudoku control + a tractable ARC subset. NOTE: decentralization-MAGNITUDE
 (close the gemma-4-12B 0.26->0.57 gap) is a .378 FOLLOW-ON. Honest null/small
 gain is a COMPLETE verdict; if still accumulating, report progress (NOT a
 retirement).

1 of 1 gate(s) failed; first failure: exp4078-verifier-reward-rft-train-launch.train_launched (actual=False == expected=True)

